Skip to Main Content2026-2027 General Catalog University of California Santa BarbaraAcademic CalendarSchedule of ClassesPrevious Catalogs Search . . . University of California Santa BarbaraCoursesProgramsDepartmentsAcademics and PoliciesIntroduction to Our CampusAcademicsPoliciesStudent LifeHome/Courses/MATRL 200S - Introduction to Structure and Phase StabilityMATRL200SDownload as PDFMATRL 200S - Introduction to Structure and Phase StabilityMaterialsCollege of EngineeringGeneralFull Course TitleIntroduction to Structure and Phase StabilityAbbreviated Course TitleINTRO STRUC & PHASEInstructor Name(s)STAFFCourse DescriptionA primer course for incoming graduate students with non-MSE background. Basic concepts of structure and descriptors: crystalline and non-crystalline solids, compounds, solid solutions. Structural imperfections: point defects, dislocations and strain fields, surfaces, interfaces. Defects in ionic crystals. Thermodynamic underpinnings of phase diagrams: phase rule, chemical potential, equilibrium conditions, metastability. Unary systems. Fundamentals of binary systems, allotropes, invariant reactions, phase fractions and compositions, relationship with structure evolution. Maps for reacting systems, Ellingham diagrams, predominance diagrams. Introduction to ternary systems: liquidus surfaces and basic invariant reactions.Units FixedUnits Fixed3Maximum number of times course can be repeated for additional credit99Maximum Units99UC Santa BarbaraSanta Barbara, California 93106(805) 893-8000Copyright © 2024 The Regents of the University of California. All Rights Reserved.Terms of Use.  Questions or Comments? Please email us.
